Title: "Writing"
Id: "801f1204-3579-4100-9373-e22f3912657e"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
Writing: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
```

```mlg-fragment
Writing:
. \"alpha :~> \alpha\"
. \"beta :~> \beta\"
Id: \"23e4567e-e89b-42d3-a456-426614174000\"
```

A collection may contain at most one top-level `Writing:` item. Each argument is
a **double-quoted** string of the form `\"name :~> body\"`: the left-hand side
must be a `Name`, and the body after `:~>` is raw, non-empty LaTeX rather than
parsed formulation syntax. The quotes are required precisely because that raw
body could otherwise be misread as a formulation.

The renderer uses these aliases when rendering names throughout expressions,
statements, and specifications. Names are split on underscores before aliases
are applied, and numeric suffix rendering honors them too, so `alpha_1` renders
as `\alpha_1` and `alpha123` renders as `\alpha_{123}`."
Id: "6d284986-b912-4519-b5d4-316e2783e35d"

SectionTitle: "Per-Item `Writing:` Sections"
Id: "bf555a15-8793-4d34-ba97-bab7031ce023"

Text: "Every top-level non-prose item — `Defines:`, `Declares:`, `Refines:`, `States:`,
`Axiom:`, `Theorem:`, `Conjecture:`, `Relation:`, and `Disambiguates:` — may
carry its own optional `Writing:` section immediately after `Aliases:`. It uses
the same double-quoted `\"name :~> body\"` form and overrides, for that item only,
how the named identifiers render. It is layered on top of the collection-wide
`Writing:` group.

```mlg-fragment
[\natural]
Defines: n
Documented:
. called: \"natural\"
Writing:
. \"pi :~> \varpi\"
Id: \"23e4567e-e89b-42d3-a456-426614174000\"
```

This is distinct from the nested `Documented:` `writing:`/`as:` item, which
controls how a mapping introduced by `Defines:` is rendered."
Id: "306c32a0-a5b6-4a0d-9406-e536d4e25673"
